455 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 317 0 R
/E (The system uses the STM8S005K6T6 microcontroller as its main control unit. It coordinates the different circuit sections and provides the required control and communication interfaces. Three 74HC165 parallel-in/serial-out shift registers are connected in a daisy-chain configuration to collect multiple input signals and transfer the captured data serially to the microcontroller. This arrangement reduces the number of direct input connections required from the controller. The output section consists of four U8C3005 ICs, which provide the required output interface for multiple cable connections.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
456 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 317 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
457 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 317 0 R
/E (The complete circuit schematic is developed using KiCad, an electronic design automation tool. The design process involves component selection, schematic symbol placement, electrical connection establishment, net labelling, and footprint assignment. The circuit is divided into functional sections, including the power supply, microcontroller, input interface, output interface, LCD, and keypad, to maintain a clear and systematic design structure. Electrical Rules Check \(ERC\) is performed to identify possible connection issues and improve the correctness of the schematic.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
