>>
endobj
689 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 328 0 R
/E (The STM8-based cable tester is an electronic system designed around the STM8S005K6T6 microcontroller. The microcontroller acts as the central control unit and provides the required interfaces for communication with the input and output sections, display and user controls.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
690 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 328 0 R
/E (The system uses three 74HC165 parallel-in serial-out shift registers in the input section. These devices allow multiple parallel input signals to be acquired and transferred serially to the microcontroller. This arrangement helps expand the number of input signals that can be handled with a limited number of microcontroller pins.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
691 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 328 0 R
/E (The output section uses four U8C3005 output driver integrated circuits to provide the required output interfacing. These devices are connected as part of the cable testing interface.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
692 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 328 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
693 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 328 0 R
/E (The system also includes a power supply circuit that accepts a 12 V input and uses a TPS563200 buck converter to generate a regulated 5 V supply for the circuit. Supporting components such as resistors, capacitors, an inductor, protection diodes and connectors are included to complete the circuit design.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
