725 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 330 0 R
/E (Cable testing is an important process used to identify faults and verify the proper functioning of electrical cables. In conventional cable testing methods, continuity is often checked manually using basic testing instruments. This process can become time-consuming and difficult when cables contain multiple wires or a large number of connections. Manual testing also requires the operator to check each connection individually, increasing the possibility of human error.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
726 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 330 0 R
/E (In cables with multiple conductors, identifying incorrect connections, open circuits, and short circuits can be challenging. A reliable testing system is therefore required to examine several cable connections systematically and provide clear information about their status.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
727 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 330 0 R
/E (The main problem addressed in this project is the development of a microcontroller-based cable tester that can simplify the testing process by automating the monitoring of cable connections. The system uses an STM8 microcontroller as the main control unit. Since the microcontroller has a limited number of input and output pins, additional interfacing circuits are required to manage multiple cable connections efficiently.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
728 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 330 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
729 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 330 0 R
/E (The project focuses on designing the complete circuit schematic using KiCad, including the microcontroller, input and output interfaces, power supply, display, keypad, and connectors. Proper component selection, circuit connections, and footprint assignment are considered during the design process.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
730 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 330 0 R
/E (Therefore, the problem is to design a compact and organized electronic cable tester circuit that can support multiple cable connections, reduce manual testing effort, and provide a foundation for an automated cable testing system.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
