/T (Data memory is used for variables such as the sampled input pattern, test mode, selected cable profile, display state and result flags. The amount of memory available places limits on the complexity of the firmware and the number of cable configurations or test records that can be stored locally.Non-volatile data storage, where available in the selected device, can be used for configuration information that must remain after power is removed. The exact memory capacities and endurance specifications should be quoted from the STMicroelectronics datasheet for the precise ordering code. Avoid transferring specifications from a related STM8 device without checking the complete part number.The clock system provides the timing reference for instruction execution and peripheral operation. The controller may support internal clock sources and, depending on the exact device and configuration, external clock components. The selected clock source affects instruction timing, serial communication timing and the delay intervals used during signal acquisition.)
/E (Data memory is used for variables such as the sampled input pattern, test mode, selected cable profile, display state and result flags. The amount of memory available places limits on the complexity of the firmware and the number of cable configurations or test records that can be stored locally.Non-volatile data storage, where available in the selected device, can be used for configuration information that must remain after power is removed. The exact memory capacities and endurance specifications should be quoted from the STMicroelectronics datasheet for the precise ordering code. Avoid transferring specifications from a related STM8 device without checking the complete part number.The clock system provides the timing reference for instruction execution and peripheral operation. The controller may support internal clock sources and, depending on the exact device and configuration, external clock components. The selected clock source affects instruction timing, serial communication timing and the delay intervals used during signal acquisition.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
915 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 339 0 R
/T (For the cable tester, clock stability is relevant to the timing of the 74HC165 clock signal, LCD communication and any other timed control sequence. The shift-register clock must meet the timing limits of the selected device. The firmware should also allow sufficient settling time between changing an output state and sampling the corresponding input.If an external crystal or resonator is used, its frequency, load capacitance and layout must follow the microcontroller manufacturer's recommendations. If the internal clock is used, its accuracy and operating range should be checked against the timing requirements of the application.The reset circuit ensures that the controller enters a known state when power is applied or when a reset condition occurs. A predictable reset state is important because the output interface should not enter an unintended condition during power-up. The reset pin connection, polarity and any external pull-up or capacitor arrangement must follow the exact device datasheet.)
/E (For the cable tester, clock stability is relevant to the timing of the 74HC165 clock signal, LCD communication and any other timed control sequence. The shift-register clock must meet the timing limits of the selected device. The firmware should also allow sufficient settling time between changing an output state and sampling the corresponding input.If an external crystal or resonator is used, its frequency, load capacitance and layout must follow the microcontroller manufacturer's recommendations. If the internal clock is used, its accuracy and operating range should be checked against the timing requirements of the application.The reset circuit ensures that the controller enters a known state when power is applied or when a reset condition occurs. A predictable reset state is important because the output interface should not enter an unintended condition during power-up. The reset pin connection, polarity and any external pull-up or capacitor arrangement must follow the exact device datasheet.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
916 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 339 0 R
/T (The controller supply must remain within its recommended operating range. Local decoupling capacitors should be placed close to the supply pins to reduce disturbances caused by switching activity inside the IC. The ground return should be short and direct. The final capacitor value and placement should be checked against the manufacturer's reference design.The GPIO allocation must cover the control signals for the 74HC165 chain, the serial data input, the output-interface control lines, LCD control and data signals, and the four keypad inputs. The SWIM programming connection must also remain accessible. A pin-allocation table helps prevent two functions from being assigned to the same pin unintentionally.For the shift-register chain, the controller is expected to control parallel loading and clocking and to read the serial output. The firmware must interpret the received bits in the correct order. For the LCD, the controller sends commands and character data. For the keypad, it reads the switch states and applies debounce logic.)
/E (The controller supply must remain within its recommended operating range. Local decoupling capacitors should be placed close to the supply pins to reduce disturbances caused by switching activity inside the IC. The ground return should be short and direct. The final capacitor value and placement should be checked against the manufacturer's reference design.The GPIO allocation must cover the control signals for the 74HC165 chain, the serial data input, the output-interface control lines, LCD control and data signals, and the four keypad inputs. The SWIM programming connection must also remain accessible. A pin-allocation table helps prevent two functions from being assigned to the same pin unintentionally.For the shift-register chain, the controller is expected to control parallel loading and clocking and to read the serial output. The firmware must interpret the received bits in the correct order. For the LCD, the controller sends commands and character data. For the keypad, it reads the switch states and applies debounce logic.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
