/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 344 0 R
/E (The control circuit adjusts the switching operation to maintain regulation. In an adjustable-output arrangement, resistor values determine the feedback voltage according to the device's specified reference and feedback equation.The feedback resistors should be placed close to the feedback pin and routed away from the switch node and inductor. Noise coupled into the feedback trace can affect regulation. The exact resistor values in the project schematic should be checked against the TI datasheet and the desired output voltage. Switching frequency affects the size of the inductor and capacitors, switching losses and electromagnetic interference. A higher frequency may permit smaller passive components but can increase switching losses. The TPS563200 operating frequency and its control behaviour should be quoted from the official datasheet. Efficiency is the ratio of output power to input power. It varies with input voltage, output current, switching losses, conduction losses and passive-component characteristics. The efficiency of the project power stage should not be stated as a fixed value without measurement or a datasheet-based calculation for the actual operating point.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
970 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 344 0 R
/E (The regulator and inductor dissipate power during operation. Thermal performance depends on copper area, board stack-up, airflow, load current and ambient temperature. The PCB should follow the manufacturer's thermal-layout recommendations and provide sufficient copper around the device where required.Protection features such as undervoltage lockout, overcurrent response and thermal shutdown are device-specific. Their existence and operating thresholds must be confirmed from the exact datasheet. The circuit should not be assumed to be protected against every possible input fault or output short.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
971 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 344 0 R
/E (The input capacitor, regulator and ground return should form a compact high-current loop. The switch-node copper should be kept appropriately small and away from sensitive signals. The inductor should be placed close to the switching node. The output capacitor should be positioned to provide a short path to the load and ground.The feedback network should sense the output at the intended point and should not be routed beside the switch node. Grounding should follow the datasheet layout guidance. A poor layout can increase ripple, noise, heating or instability even if the schematic is correct.The TPS563200-based stage is intended to generate the 5 V rail from the nominal 12 V input. This rail supports the digital and interface circuits according to their supply requirements. The final load calculation must include the LCD backlight and all connected devices.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
972 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 344 0 R
/E (The output voltage, ripple, start-up behaviour and thermal performance must be verified after the board is fabricated. Initial power-up should use a current-limited bench supply. The load should be increased gradually while monitoring the output voltage and device temperature.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
