/E (The schematic symbol and physical footprint must also maintain consistent pin numbering to avoid incorrect electrical connections. Each pin of the U8C3005G device should be verified against the manufacturer's datasheet, including supply pins, ground pins, input pins, output pins, and control pins. The pin configuration must not be assumed based on the visual arrangement of the schematic symbol because the actual physical pin arrangement may differ. In KiCad, the footprint pad numbers must correspond exactly to the pin numbers assigned to the schematic symbol. Any mismatch between the symbol and footprint can result in signals being connected to unintended physical terminals, potentially affecting the operation of the complete circuit. Therefore, symbol verification, pin mapping, and footprint compatibility are important design review activities, particularly when using custom or supplier-specific component libraries.)
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
1038 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 350 0 R
/E (The electrical characteristics of the U8C3005G must be obtained from a reliable manufacturer datasheet or supplier document before completing the hardware design. Important parameters include the device function, pin configuration, recommended operating supply voltage, input logic thresholds, output voltage and current limits, absolute maximum ratings, operating temperature range, power dissipation, and thermal resistance. Since these devices are included in the output section of the cable tester, their output configuration and behaviour under different load conditions must also be examined. It is necessary to determine whether the outputs are push-pull, open-drain, open-collector, or another configuration because these characteristics influence the selection of pull-up or pull-down resistors, output loading, protection circuitry, and firmware control requirements. The device must also be evaluated for its behaviour under open-load, short-circuit, and incorrect cable connection conditions to ensure that it can operate safely within the intended application.)
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1039 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 350 0 R
/E (The output section is connected to external cable conductors and must therefore be considered an important electrical interface of the cable testing system. The voltage and current applied to individual cable pins, the maximum number of simultaneously active outputs, and the possible effects of incorrect cable wiring must be considered during the design process. In situations where two output connections become electrically connected through an incorrectly wired or shorted cable, excessive current may flow and damage the connected components. Suitable protection techniques, such as current-limiting resistors, series resistance, protection components, or controlled testing sequences, may be required depending on the verified electrical characteristics of the device. The supply voltage and current requirements must also be confirmed from the datasheet, and appropriate local decoupling capacitors should be provided near the supply pins as recommended by the manufacturer to maintain stable operating conditions and reduce unwanted supply noise.)
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
