/T (The power supply circuit is implemented using the TPS563200 buck converter. The circuit accepts a 12 V DC input and generates a regulated 5 V output. The required supporting components, including the inductor, input capacitors, output capacitors, and feedback resistors, are included in the schematic. The components are connected according to the buck converter configuration.)
/E (The power supply circuit is implemented using the TPS563200 buck converter. The circuit accepts a 12 V DC input and generates a regulated 5 V output. The required supporting components, including the inductor, input capacitors, output capacitors, and feedback resistors, are included in the schematic. The components are connected according to the buck converter configuration.)
/Pg 52 0 R
/K [3]
>>
