1158 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 359 0 R
/E (The STM8 microcontroller circuit forms the central control section of the proposed cable testing system. The STM8S005K6T6 microcontroller is used as the main processing unit responsible for coordinating the operations of different hardware sections. It provides the necessary input and output interfaces for communication with peripheral devices, including input shift registers, output interface circuits, LCD, and keypad. The microcontroller receives input signals, processes the information, and controls the corresponding output operations required for cable testing. Its multiple GPIO pins are utilized to establish communication with the different circuit sections and manage the overall testing process.)
/Pg 55 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1159 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 359 0 R
/E (The microcontroller circuit includes several supporting components to ensure stable and reliable operation. A clock circuit is provided to generate the timing reference required for microcontroller operation. The crystal oscillator is connected with suitable capacitors to support clock generation and maintain stable timing. Reset circuitry is incorporated to initialize the microcontroller and ensure proper startup during power-up or manual reset conditions. Resistors and capacitors are used in the supporting sections to establish the required electrical conditions and improve circuit stability. These components collectively support the proper functioning of the microcontroller and its associated peripherals.)
/Pg 55 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1160 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 359 0 R
/E (Power supply connections are provided to operate the microcontroller and its associated peripheral circuits. Decoupling capacitors are connected near the supply pins to minimize unwanted voltage fluctuations and reduce electrical noise. The microcontroller's input and output pins are connected to the corresponding circuit sections through appropriate signal connections. These connections enable communication with the input shift registers and output interface circuits, while additional connections support LCD display and keypad operations. The programming interface is also included to facilitate firmware loading and debugging during the development process.)
/Pg 55 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1161 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 359 0 R
/E (The complete STM8 microcontroller circuit schematic, including the microcontroller, clock circuit, reset arrangement, power connections, and associated interfacing sections, is shown in Fig. 4.2. The schematic illustrates the arrangement of the essential components and their electrical connections required for the operation of the controller section. This circuit serves as the foundation for integrating the different functional blocks of the cable testing system and supports subsequent PCB implementation, firmware development, and hardware testing.)
/Pg 55 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
