/E (4.5 Power Supply Circuit Implementation)
/Pg 59 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
1200 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 363 0 R
/T (4.5 Power Supply Circuit Implementation)
/E (4.5 Power Supply Circuit Implementation)
/Pg 59 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1201 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 363 0 R
/E (The power supply circuit is an important section of the STM8-based cable testing system, as it provides the required operating voltage to the microcontroller and other peripheral components. The circuit is designed to accept a 12 V DC input and convert it into a regulated 5 V DC output using a buck converter. The TPS563200 switching regulator IC is used for voltage conversion, providing an efficient step-down power supply for the overall system.)
/Pg 59 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1202 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 363 0 R
/E (The input supply is connected through a power connector, followed by a diode arrangement that provides input protection. Input filtering capacitors are connected to reduce unwanted voltage fluctuations and provide a stable supply to the regulator. These components help improve the reliability of the power supply section and protect the downstream circuit from input disturbances.)
/Pg 59 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1203 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 363 0 R
/E (The TPS563200 buck converter operates by switching the input supply and controlling the energy transferred to the output. An inductor is connected at the switching output to store and transfer energy, while capacitors are used for filtering and reducing output voltage ripple. The feedback network, consisting of resistors, is connected to the regulator to maintain the required output voltage. This arrangement enables the conversion of the 12 V input into a regulated 5 V supply suitable for the microcontroller and other circuit sections.)
/Pg 59 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1204 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 363 0 R
/E (Additional capacitors are provided at the output to improve voltage stability and reduce fluctuations during circuit operation. A diode and LED indicator arrangement is also included in the output section to provide visual indication of the power supply status. The regulated 5 V output is distributed to the required hardware sections of the cable tester. Proper selection of the inductor, capacitors, resistors, and protection components is important for maintaining stable power delivery and reliable circuit operation.)
/Pg 59 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1205 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 363 0 R
/E (The complete power supply circuit schematic, showing the input connector, diode arrangement, filtering components, TPS563200 buck converter, feedback network, and regulated output section, is presented in Fig. 4.5. This circuit provides the necessary power conversion and distribution required for the operation of the STM8-based cable testing system.)
/Pg 59 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
