endobj
1223 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 365 0 R
/T (4.6 Input Interface Circuit Implementation)
/E (4.6 Input Interface Circuit Implementation)
/Pg 61 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1224 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 365 0 R
/E (The input interface circuit is designed to receive and process multiple input signals from the cable connections under test. It consists of three 74HC165 parallel-in serial-out \(PISO\) shift registers that allow multiple input signals to be monitored using a limited number of microcontroller pins. Each 74HC165 IC provides eight parallel input channels, allowing the three devices to handle a total of 24 input signals. This arrangement reduces the number of GPIO connections required from the STM8S005K6T6 microcontroller and simplifies the overall circuit design.)
/Pg 61 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1225 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 365 0 R
/E (The 74HC165 shift registers capture the input signals simultaneously through their parallel input pins and transfer the stored data serially to the microcontroller. The parallel load and clock control signals are used to manage the data acquisition and shifting operations. The serial output of the shift registers provides the input information to the microcontroller, which can process the received data to determine the connection status of the cable under test. The three shift registers are connected through their respective control and data lines to support the sequential reading of multiple input channels.)
/Pg 61 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1226 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 365 0 R
/E (The input circuit also includes resistor networks and connectors for establishing the required input connections. The resistor networks help provide suitable electrical conditions for the input signal lines, while the connectors provide interfaces for connecting the cable conductors to the testing circuit. Decoupling capacitors are connected near the shift register supply pins to reduce supply noise and maintain stable operation. The shift registers operate using the regulated 5 V supply, with their ground connections connected to the common circuit ground.)
/Pg 61 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1227 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 365 0 R
/E (The complete input interface circuit, consisting of three 74HC165 shift registers, associated resistor networks, input connectors, and supporting components, is shown in Fig. 4.6. This arrangement enables the system to acquire multiple cable input signals efficiently and transfer the collected information to the STM8 microcontroller for further processing and cable fault identification.)
/Pg 61 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
