/Pg 63 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
1245 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 367 0 R
/E (The output interface circuit is designed to generate and control the required output signals for the STM8-based cable testing system. It consists of four U8C3005G devices in SOP-16 packages, which are connected to the output section of the circuit. These devices receive control and data signals from the microcontroller through the corresponding signal lines. The arrangement provides multiple output connections required for interfacing with the cable under test.)
/Pg 63 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1246 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 367 0 R
/E (The four U8C3005G devices are connected through common control signals and individual data connections. Signals such as serial data, clock, and load are provided to coordinate the operation of the output section. The supply voltage and ground connections are provided to each device to ensure proper operation. Capacitors are connected near the supply pins of the integrated circuits to reduce supply noise and maintain stable operating conditions. These supporting components help improve the reliability of the output interface.)
/Pg 63 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1247 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 367 0 R
/E (The output connections from the interface circuit are brought to a multi-pin connector, which provides the required connection points for the cable under test. The individual output lines are organized and connected according to the intended cable pin configuration. This arrangement allows the output section to work together with the input interface circuit during the cable testing process. The microcontroller coordinates the operation of the output section by providing the required control signals and processing the corresponding input information.)
/Pg 63 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1248 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 367 0 R
/E (The complete output interface circuit, showing the four U8C3005G devices, associated data and control connections, decoupling capacitors, and output connector, is illustrated in Fig. 4.7. This circuit forms an important part of the cable testing system by providing the required output connections for carrying out cable continuity and connection testing.)
/Pg 63 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
