/T (The KiCad 3D Viewer is an important tool used to visualize the physical appearance of a printed circuit board \(PCB\) before fabrication and assembly. It provides a three-dimensional representation of the board, including component bodies, connectors, mounting holes and other mechanical features. This visualization helps the designer understand how the selected components are positioned on the PCB and how the overall board may appear after assembly.In the STM8-based cable tester project, the 3D Viewer was used to inspect the PCB design after the schematic information and component footprints had been transferred to the PCB editor. The viewer displays the board with its assigned footprints and available 3D models, providing a realistic representation of the proposed hardware arrangement.)
/E (The KiCad 3D Viewer is an important tool used to visualize the physical appearance of a printed circuit board \(PCB\) before fabrication and assembly. It provides a three-dimensional representation of the board, including component bodies, connectors, mounting holes and other mechanical features. This visualization helps the designer understand how the selected components are positioned on the PCB and how the overall board may appear after assembly.In the STM8-based cable tester project, the 3D Viewer was used to inspect the PCB design after the schematic information and component footprints had been transferred to the PCB editor. The viewer displays the board with its assigned footprints and available 3D models, providing a realistic representation of the proposed hardware arrangement.)
/Pg 67 0 R
/K [5]
>>
