1447 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 378 0 R
/E (Correct PCB footprint selection is essential for ensuring proper component mounting and reliable soldering during assembly. It prevents pad-number and pin-mapping errors, maintains suitable spacing between neighbouring components and supports accurate PCB manufacturing. Incorrect footprint selection can lead to component misalignment, improper solder connections and electrical connectivity problems. Therefore, footprint assignment and verification form an important part of the PCB design process.)
/Pg 74 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1448 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 378 0 R
/E (Correct PCB footprint assignment ensures that the physical package of each electronic component matches its schematic symbol and electrical pin configuration. In the STM8-based cable tester, appropriate footprint selection for the microcontroller, shift registers, power converter, output devices, display, switches and connectors provides the foundation for the subsequent PCB placement, routing and fabrication stages.)
/Pg 74 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
