/T (The developed schematic demonstrates how different electronic components can be integrated to form a microcontroller-based cable tester. The modular design approach makes it easier to understand the role of each circuit section and the connections between them.One of the important design considerations was the handling of multiple input signals. Directly connecting a large number of input signals to the microcontroller would require several GPIO pins. The use of three 74HC165 shift registers provides an alternative arrangement in which multiple parallel signals are converted into serial data. The daisy-chain configuration further simplifies the connection between the shift registers and the microcontroller.)
/E (The developed schematic demonstrates how different electronic components can be integrated to form a microcontroller-based cable tester. The modular design approach makes it easier to understand the role of each circuit section and the connections between them.One of the important design considerations was the handling of multiple input signals. Directly connecting a large number of input signals to the microcontroller would require several GPIO pins. The use of three 74HC165 shift registers provides an alternative arrangement in which multiple parallel signals are converted into serial data. The daisy-chain configuration further simplifies the connection between the shift registers and the microcontroller.)
/Pg 80 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
