/T (The LCD and keypad provide a basic user interface. The 4-bit LCD connection reduces the number of microcontroller pins needed for display communication. The tactile switches provide additional input connections for user interaction.KiCad played an important role in the implementation process. Its schematic editor allowed the circuit to be divided into functional blocks and connected using wires and net labels. Footprint assignment helped associate the selected components with their physical packages. ERC provided a method for identifying possible electrical connection issues.)
