2898 0 obj
<<
/Title (The developed schematic demonstrates how different electronic components can be integrated to form a microcontroller-based cable tester. The modular design approach makes it easier to understand the role of each circuit section and the connections between them.One of the important design considerations was the handling of multiple input signals. Directly connecting a large number of input signals to the microcontroller would require several GPIO pins. The use of three 74HC165 shift registers provides an alternative arrangement in which multiple parallel signals are converted into serial data. The daisy-chain configuration further simplifies the connection between the shift registers and the microcontroller.)
/Dest [80 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2625 0 R
/Next 3171 0 R
>>
endobj
2899 0 obj
<<
/Title (July 2026 - Dec 2026)
/Dest [80 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2625 0 R
/Prev 3172 0 R
>>
endobj
2900 0 obj
<<
/Title (The LCD interface can also be programmed to provide clear and understandable information about the cable testing process. It can display the testing status, detected connection conditions, and relevant error messages to help the user identify faults without requiring external measuring instruments. The keypad can be utilized to provide user input and control different testing operations, making the system more convenient and interactive. Once the PCB fabrication, component assembly, and firmware development are completed, the complete hardware can undergo functional testing and validation using cables with different connection configurations. The power supply section, microcontroller operation, input and output interfaces, display functionality, and overall circuit performance can be evaluated under different operating conditions to verify the reliability and accuracy of the proposed system.)
/Dest [82 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1604 0 R
/Prev 2627 0 R
/Next 2901 0 R
>>
endobj
2901 0 obj
<<
/Title (Further improvements can focus on reducing power consumption, improving reliability, and supporting different cable types. Additional features can enhance testing speed and fault detection, making the system more efficient and user-friendly.)
/Dest [82 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1604 0 R
/Prev 2900 0 R
/Next 2628 0 R
>>
endobj
