/Title (The controller supply must remain within its recommended operating range. Local decoupling capacitors should be placed close to the supply pins to reduce disturbances caused by switching activity inside the IC. The ground return should be short and direct. The final capacitor value and placement should be checked against the manufacturer's reference design.The GPIO allocation must cover the control signals for the 74HC165 chain, the serial data input, the output-interface control lines, LCD control and data signals, and the four keypad inputs. The SWIM programming connection must also remain accessible. A pin-allocation table helps prevent two functions from being assigned to the same pin unintentionally.For the shift-register chain, the controller is expected to control parallel loading and clocking and to read the serial output. The firmware must interpret the received bits in the correct order. For the LCD, the controller sends commands and character data. For the keypad, it reads the switch states and applies debounce logic.)
