/Title (The STM8 family uses the Single Wire Interface Module \(SWIM\) for programming and debugging. The project schematic includes a programming header intended to provide access to this interface. The header must be wired according to the selected programmer's documentation and the microcontroller pinout.The programming connector should be accessible after the PCB is assembled. It should be labelled clearly and should not be placed where the cable or enclosure blocks access. Before connecting a programmer, verify the ground reference, signal pin and target-voltage arrangement.The STM8S005K6T6CTR is intended to execute the cable-test control sequence. A future firmware implementation may initialize the LCD, wait for a user command, select an output path, capture the input state through the shift-register chain and compare the observed result against the expected cable map. It may then display a pass, open, short or mismatch indication if the hardware can distinguish those conditions.)
/Dest [36 0 R /Fit]
